---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const LIVE_DASHBOARD_URL = "https://mtg.alejandroojedacelis.com/superset/dashboard/p/Z285PRNgp1Y/?standalone=3";
---

<BaseLayout 
  description="Historical print data analysis for Magic: The Gathering legendary creatures built with Scryfall JSONL datasets, DuckDB, and Apache Superset." 
  title="Magic: The Gathering Analytics | Alejandro Ojeda-Celis"
>
  <main class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center justify-between gap-4 mb-8 pb-6 border-b border-neutral-800">
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-2 text-white">MTG Legendary Creature Evolution</h1>
        <p class="text-neutral-400">
          Historical printing trends and set-by-set distribution analytics powered by DuckDB and Apache Superset.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <a 
          href="https://github.com/Digiyumon" 
          target="_blank" 
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-neutral-800 hover:bg-neutral-700 text-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl border border-neutral-700 transition font-medium text-sm whitespace-nowrap shadow-sm"
        >
          GitHub Repo →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <br>
    <!-- Project Context & Live Demo Section -->
    <section class="mb-12 space-y-6">
      
      <!-- Context & Login Info Card -->
      <div class="p-8 rounded-2xl border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/60 backdrop-blur shadow-2xl space-y-6">
        
        <!-- Context Note -->
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-300 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2">
          <p class="font-medium">
            This dashboard was created in September 2026 prior to the release of the <em>Reality Fracture</em> expansion set.
          </p>
          <p>
            It was built to explore a simple question: <em>"Driven by the rising popularity of the Commander format, how has the printing rate of Legendary Creatures evolved over time?"</em>
          </p>
          <p>
            What started as a single query turned into a broader exploration of MTG design shifts across decades of set releases. I hope you find the dataset insights as fascinating as I did!
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Description & Login Box Grid -->
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 items-center">
          <div class="md:col-span-2 space-y-2">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Interactive Superset Analytics Board</h2>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Access the full analytical workspace directly on my homelab infrastructure via Cloudflare Tunnel. Filter by set releases, legendary creature power scales, and color identities in real time.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Styled Guest Credentials Box -->
            No need to log in. Just click on "Dashboards" on the top of the window and click on the "MTG Legendary Creatures Data Visualization" dashboard. 
          </div>
        </div>


      <!-- Live iFrame Container -->
      <div class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900 shadow-2xl overflow-hidden">
        <iframe height="1000px" width="90%"
          src="http://mtg.alejandroojedacelis.com/superset/dashboard/p/Z285PRNgp1Y/"
          title="Apache Superset MTG Dashboard"
          loading="lazy"
          allowfullscreen
        ></iframe>
      </div>

    </section>

    <!-- Pipeline Architecture Breakdown -->
    <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
      <div class="md:col-span-2 space-y-6 text-neutral-300">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Architecture & Analytical Objective</h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            This pipeline parses bulk JSONL records from Scryfall to evaluate card design shifts across decades of Magic: The Gathering releases.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2">Engineering Highlights</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-neutral-400 text-sm">
            <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">DuckDB Engine:</strong> High-speed columnar SQL parsing of raw card attributes.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Proxmox Hosting:</strong> Containerized Apache Superset stack hosted on local homelab hardware.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-neutral-200">Cloudflare Tunnel:</strong> Secure Zero-Trust outbound routing eliminating open router ports.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Tech Stack Sidebar -->
      <div class="p-6 bg-neutral-900/40 border border-neutral-800 rounded-xl h-fit">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-4">Pipeline Stack</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-neutral-400">
          <li class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-neutral-800/80 pb-2">
            <span>Database</span>
            <span class="text-white font-medium">DuckDB</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-neutral-800/80 pb-2">
            <span>BI Platform</span>
            <span class="text-white font-medium">Apache Superset</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-neutral-800/80 pb-2">
            <span>Tunneling</span>
            <span class="text-white font-medium">Cloudflare Tunnel</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span>Data Ingestion</span>
            <span class="text-white font-medium">Scryfall JSONL</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>